-- New York law has read this against the source.
--
-- Seat: a developer asking whether it is a frontier developer, a large one, and
-- whether an event is a critical safety incident.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/ny-s8828-2026-ch-96.txt; `src:N` is line N.
-- The source keeps the bill's own line numbers and hyphenation, so a quoted line
-- begins with the bill's line number. Target compiler: main. Forks are in NOTES.md.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `raise-domain`

§ `Section 1420 -- Definitions`

§§ `1, 2: affiliate, artificial intelligence model`

-- "Affiliate" is used only in subdivision 10; the developer states its revenue
-- together with its affiliates as one figure. Whether a system is an "artificial
-- intelligence model" is asked as a fact, because the definition is a description.
-- src:89 | 41 1. "Affiliate" means a person controlling, controlled by, or under
-- src:90 | 42 common control with a specified person, directly or indirectly, through
-- src:91 | 43 one or more intermediaries.
-- src:92 | 44 2. "Artificial intelligence model" means an engineered or machine-
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(2) (src:89-92)
GIVEN m IS A `me and my model`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the model is an AI model within the article` m MEANS
    m's `the model is an artificial intelligence model`

§§ `6: foundation model`

-- src:136 | 34 6. "Foundation model" means an artificial intelligence model that is
-- src:137 | 35 all of the following:
-- src:138 | 36 (a) trained on a broad data set;
-- src:139 | 37 (b) designed for generality of output; and
-- src:140 | 38 (c) adaptable to a wide range of distinctive tasks.
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(6) (src:136-140)
GIVEN m IS A `me and my model`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the model is a foundation model` m IF
        `the model is an AI model within the article` m
    AND m's `the model was trained on a broad data set`
    AND m's `the model is designed for generality of output`
    AND m's `the model is adaptable to a wide range of distinctive tasks`

§§ `9: frontier model`

-- "greater than 10§26": the deposited page prints the exponent mark as a section
-- sign; read as 10^26 (F12). Exactly 10^26 operations is not enough (F2).
-- src:148 | 46 9. (a) "Frontier model" means a foundation model that was trained
-- src:149 | 47 using a quantity of computing power greater than 10§26 integer or float-
-- src:150 | 48 ing-point operations.
-- src:151 | 49 (b) The quantity of computing power described in paragraph (a) of this
-- src:152 | 50 subdivision shall include computing for the original training run and
-- src:153 | 51 for any subsequent fine-tuning, reinforcement learning, or other materi-
-- src:154 | 52 al modifications the developer applies to a preceding foundation model.
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(9) (src:148-154)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the computing power threshold, in operations` MEANS 100000000000000000000000000

-- "was trained using": the operations already used, including later fine-tuning,
-- reinforcement learning and other material modifications (9)(b). A model whose
-- training has begun but has not yet used more than 10^26 operations is not yet a
-- frontier model, even if the developer intends to go past it (F3).
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(9) (src:148-154)
GIVEN m IS A `me and my model`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the model is a frontier model` m IF
        `the model is a foundation model` m
    AND m's `the operations used to train the model so far` GREATER THAN `the computing power threshold, in operations`

§§ `8: frontier developer`

-- "has trained, or initiated the training of, a frontier model, with respect to which
-- the person has used, or intends to use, at least as much computing power ... as
-- would meet the technical specifications found in subdivision nine". Read as: the
-- developer has trained or begun training a foundation model for which the operations
-- it has used, or intends to use, are more than 10^26 (F3). The developer states the
-- largest such figure over all its foundation models. A developer whose model has
-- already used more than 10^26 operations is one in any case.
-- src:143 | 41 8. "Frontier developer" means a person who has trained, or initiated
-- src:144 | 42 the training of, a frontier model, with respect to which the person has
-- src:145 | 43 used, or intends to use, at least as much computing power to train the
-- src:146 | 44 frontier model as would meet the technical specifications found in
-- src:147 | 45 subdivision nine of this section.
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(8) (src:143-147)
GIVEN m IS A `me and my model`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am a frontier developer` m IF
       m's `the most operations I have used or intend to use to train any foundation model I have trained or begun to train` GREATER THAN `the computing power threshold, in operations`
    OR (    m's `I have trained, or initiated the training of, the model`
        AND `the model is a frontier model` m)

-- "its frontier models" (section 1422(3)(a)): a frontier model the developer trained
-- or began to train.
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(8), (9) (src:143-147)
GIVEN m IS A `me and my model`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the model is a frontier model of mine` m IF
        m's `I have trained, or initiated the training of, the model`
    AND `the model is a frontier model` m

§§ `10: large frontier developer`

-- "in excess of five hundred million dollars": exactly $500,000,000 is not enough (F2).
-- "the preceding calendar year" is not anchored to a date in the text (F15).
-- src:155 | 53 10. "Large frontier developer" means a frontier developer that togeth-
-- src:156 | 54 er with its affiliates collectively had annual gross revenues in excess
-- src:157 | 55 of five hundred million dollars in the preceding calendar year.
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(1), (10) (src:155-157)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the revenue threshold, in dollars` MEANS 500000000

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(1), (10) (src:155-157)
GIVEN m IS A `me and my model`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am a large frontier developer` m IF
        `I am a frontier developer` m
    AND m's `the annual gross revenues of me and my affiliates in the preceding calendar year` GREATER THAN `the revenue threshold, in dollars`

§§ `3 and section 1423: catastrophic risk`

-- A catastrophic risk is a RISK; kind (b) of critical safety incident is "harm
-- resulting from the materialization of" one. Read as: the event the risk describes
-- has happened -- a frontier model, doing one of (i) to (iii), materially contributed
-- to the death of or serious injury to more than 50 people, or to more than
-- $1,000,000,000 of damage to or loss of property, arising from a single incident --
-- and none of the exclusions in (3)(b) applies (F5). Loss of value of equity is not
-- property damage (section 1423); the developer leaves it out of the dollar figure.
-- src:96 | 48 3. (a) "Catastrophic risk" means a foreseeable and material risk that
-- src:97 | 49 a frontier developer's development, storage, use, or deployment of a
-- src:98 | 50 frontier model will materially contribute to the death of, or serious
-- src:99 | 51 injury to, more than fifty people or more than one billion dollars in
-- src:100 | 52 damage to, or loss of, property arising from a single incident involving
-- src:101 | 53 a frontier model doing any of the following:
-- src:102 | S. 8828 3
-- src:103 | 1 (i) providing expert-level assistance in the creation or release of a
-- src:104 | 2 chemical, biological, radiological, or nuclear weapon;
-- src:105 | 3 (ii) engaging in conduct with no meaningful human oversight, inter-
-- src:106 | 4 vention, or supervision that is either a cyberattack or, if the conduct
-- src:107 | 5 had been committed by a human, would constitute the crime of murder,
-- src:108 | 6 assault, extortion, or theft, including theft by false pretense; or
-- src:109 | 7 (iii) evading the control of its frontier developer or user.
-- src:110 | 8 (b) "Catastrophic risk" does not include a foreseeable and material
-- src:111 | 9 risk from any of the following:
-- src:112 | 10 (i) information that a frontier model outputs if the information is
-- src:113 | 11 otherwise publicly accessible in a substantially similar form from a
-- src:114 | 12 source other than a foundation model;
-- src:115 | 13 (ii) lawful activity of the federal government; or
-- src:116 | 14 (iii) harm caused by a frontier model in combination with other soft-
-- src:117 | 15 ware if the frontier model did not materially contribute to the harm.
-- src:375 | 46 § 1423. Loss of equity. The loss of value of equity shall not count as
-- src:376 | 47 damage to or loss of property for the purposes of this article.
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(3) and § 1423 (src:96-117) (src:375-376)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the people threshold` MEANS 50

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(3)(a) (src:96-101)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the property threshold, in dollars` MEANS 1000000000

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(3)(a)(i) to (iii) (src:103-109)
GIVEN c IS A `what the model did`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the conduct is of a kind in (3)(a)` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `none of the three kinds of conduct` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The facts of the event, before asking whether the model is a frontier model.
-- (3)(b)(iii), harm from the model in combination with other software where the model
-- did not materially contribute, is covered by the requirement in (3)(a) that the
-- model "materially contribute"; it needs no separate fact.
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(3) and § 1423 (src:96-117) (src:375-376)
GIVEN i IS A `the incident as I know it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the facts fit the materialization of a catastrophic risk` i IF
        `the conduct is of a kind in (3)(a)` (i's `the model's conduct`)
    AND i's `the model materially contributed to the deaths, injuries, or damage`
    AND i's `the deaths, injuries, or damage arose from a single incident`
    AND (    i's `the number of people who died or were seriously injured` GREATER THAN `the people threshold`
         OR i's `the dollars of damage to, or loss of, property` GREATER THAN `the property threshold, in dollars`)
    AND (NOT i's `the harm came from information the model output that is otherwise publicly accessible in a substantially similar form from a source other than a foundation model`)
    AND (NOT i's `the harm came from lawful activity of the federal government`)

§§ `4: critical safety incident`

-- Each kind names "a frontier model", so an event with a model that is not (yet) a
-- frontier model is no critical safety incident (F3). The kinds may overlap; every
-- kind that applies is listed (F6).
-- src:118 | 16 4. "Critical safety incident" means any of the following:
-- src:119 | 17 (a) unauthorized access to, modification of, or exfiltration of, the
-- src:120 | 18 model weights of a frontier model that results in death or bodily inju-
-- src:121 | 19 ry;
-- src:122 | 20 (b) harm resulting from the materialization of a catastrophic risk;
-- src:123 | 21 (c) loss of control of a frontier model causing death or bodily inju-
-- src:124 | 22 ry; or
-- src:125 | 23 (d) a frontier model that uses deceptive techniques against the fron-
-- src:126 | 24 tier developer to subvert the controls or monitoring of its frontier
-- src:127 | 25 developer outside of the context of an evaluation designed to elicit
-- src:128 | 26 this behavior and in a manner that demonstrates materially increased
-- src:129 | 27 catastrophic risk.
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(4), (4)(a) (src:118-129)
GIVEN i IS A `the incident as I know it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the facts fit kind (a)` i IF
        i's `there was unauthorized access to, modification of, or exfiltration of the model weights`
    AND i's `that access, modification, or exfiltration resulted in death or bodily injury`

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(4)(b) (src:122)
GIVEN i IS A `the incident as I know it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the facts fit kind (b)` i IF
    `the facts fit the materialization of a catastrophic risk` i

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(4)(c) (src:123-124)
GIVEN i IS A `the incident as I know it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the facts fit kind (c)` i IF
        i's `there was a loss of control of the model`
    AND i's `the loss of control caused death or bodily injury`

-- "outside of the context of an evaluation designed to elicit this behavior", and
-- "in a manner that demonstrates materially increased catastrophic risk", a judgment
-- the developer states as a fact.
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(4)(d) (src:125-129)
GIVEN i IS A `the incident as I know it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the facts fit kind (d)` i IF
        i's `the model used deceptive techniques against me to subvert my controls or monitoring`
    AND (NOT i's `that happened in an evaluation designed to elicit that behavior`)
    AND i's `that behavior demonstrates materially increased catastrophic risk`

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(4) (src:118-129)
GIVEN k IS A `a kind of critical safety incident`, i IS A `the incident as I know it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the facts fit the kind` k i MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `kind (a), unauthorized access to, modification of, or exfiltration of model weights resulting in death or bodily injury` THEN `the facts fit kind (a)` i
    WHEN `kind (b), harm resulting from the materialization of a catastrophic risk` THEN `the facts fit kind (b)` i
    WHEN `kind (c), loss of control of a frontier model causing death or bodily injury` THEN `the facts fit kind (c)` i
    WHEN `kind (d), deceptive subversion of the developer's controls or monitoring` THEN `the facts fit kind (d)` i

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(4) (src:118-129)
GIVEN m IS A `me and my model`, i IS A `the incident as I know it`
GIVETH A LIST OF `a kind of critical safety incident`
`the kinds of critical safety incident that apply` m i MEANS
    IF `the model is a frontier model` m
    THEN filter (GIVEN k YIELD `the facts fit the kind` k i)
                (LIST `kind (a), unauthorized access to, modification of, or exfiltration of model weights resulting in death or bodily injury`
                    , `kind (b), harm resulting from the materialization of a catastrophic risk`
                    , `kind (c), loss of control of a frontier model causing death or bodily injury`
                    , `kind (d), deceptive subversion of the developer's controls or monitoring`)
    ELSE LIST

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(4) (src:118-129)
GIVEN m IS A `me and my model`, i IS A `the incident as I know it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a critical safety incident` m i IF
        `the model is a frontier model` m
    AND (   `the facts fit kind (a)` i
         OR `the facts fit kind (b)` i
         OR `the facts fit kind (c)` i
         OR `the facts fit kind (d)` i)

§§ `5, 7, 11 to 16: deploy, frontier AI framework, model weight, and the rest`

-- Inert for reporting. Nothing in section 1422(3) turns on whether the model has been
-- deployed: the duty is for any critical safety incident "pertaining to one or more of
-- its frontier models" (F7). "Model weight" and "property" are glosses on kinds (a)
-- and (b); "person" (14) and the department, superintendent and office (12, 15, 16)
-- name who is bound and who receives the report.
